WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.153
Teacher midterm practice, question 8.

2
00:00:03.773 --> 00:00:06.329
In Figure 1, what does point D indicate?

3
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.531
D is the highest point on the engineering stress strain curve.

4
00:00:12.151 --> 00:00:14.479
The maximum engineering stress is the ultimate

5
00:00:14.479 --> 00:00:17.211
tensile strength, and necking begins there.

6
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.929
The answer is B: tensile strength.

7
00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:24.685
Fracture, at F, is not the strongest point.

8
00:00:24.685 --> 00:00:28.431
After D the engineering stress falls, because the neck shrinks.
